  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Nature and Description
    
    A bone relic of divine origin, carved from the jaw of the dead god worshipped by the orca pods. The summary registry describes the Tooth as larger than an adult orca; the chronicle accounts consistently report it as the length of a penguin's forearm. I note the discrepancy without resolving it. Objects associated with pressure-magic have been documented as resisting consistent measurement, and the orca pressure-song tradition does not distinguish between physical and ritual magnitude. It is yellowed like old ice, ridged with grooves — some original to the divine jaw, others scored into the bone during the Abyss Collapse Tide, when the deep waters surrounding the Berg underwent catastrophic thermal collapse and the ocean floor buckled.
    
    The Tooth hums. Not audibly — it exerts a pressure against the inner ear, a vibration carried through water at frequencies that precede sound. Those who have held it report the same dream: drowning in warm darkness while something vast watches with patient hunger. Not threatening. Patient. The orca theological position is unambiguous: the Tooth still dreams because the god does. Its resonance persists because the source has not fully stopped.
    
    No penguin has held the Tooth. Achaiwei Rukar'Crest, an orca-contact negotiator of the Frozen Peace era, heard the hum from forty spans away and refused to approach closer.
    
    ## Origin
    
    In orca creation tradition, the Tooth was pried from the divine mandible by **Rrak-gruk-krul the Jaw-Breaker**, the first orca shaman, who dove into the open wound while the god's blood was still cooling. The name survives only in the oldest pressure-songs and is officially forgotten — a designation whose implications I leave to scholars of orca liturgical suppression. The Tooth is held as proof that the god had jaws, was flesh, was kin. The orca do not classify it as an artifact. They classify it as an amputation.
    
    In the primordial age, **Grandmother Deep**, an ancient orca matriarch and one of the three divine shapers who maintained the Berg, carried the Tooth in her own jaw. The boundary between her body and the instrument was, by the accounts, a distinction only later scholars would need to make. When Grandmother Deep pressed the Tooth's hum against the **Omega Obelisk** — a whale-bone relic older than all three primordial shapers — the deep did not answer for the first time in her long memory. This detail appears in only one source, *The Holding of the Berg*, and is not corroborated by ice-memory at any depth I have been able to reach.
    
    ## Properties and Cost
    
    Wielders gain dominion over pressure-magic: the ability to collapse lungs, to read the weight of the deep like language, to speak to things that have not surfaced in centuries. The **Wake-Singers**, the orca shamanic order that serves as the Tooth's primary custodians, use it to focus their blood-rituals and amplify their hunt-songs into pressure-waves capable of shattering ice and bending water.
    
    The cost accumulates in the bones. An increasing compulsion to feed the ocean. A hunger that begins as curiosity and ends as inevitability. Three shamans have carried the Tooth into the depths and never surfaced. The first lasted four days before the compulsion took her. The second survived a week — witnesses report she was singing when she went under, and the sound cracked ice. The third walked in during the Orca Incursion and did not return; whether she drowned or found what she sought remains unclear.
    
    ## Custody
    
    The Tooth's chain of possession is tangled. The Wake-Singers keep it at the **Corpse Current**, the deep-sea location where the dead god's influence pools thickest, but it has passed through other hands:
    
    - **Hainou mewei'Frostglass**, an Aurora Stack practitioner, first encountered the Tooth in the crystal passages near Bastion Apex within Aurora Berg. Contact with the relic radiated the **Snowdrift-numb technique** — a meditative practice for reading or altering ice-memory, at the cost of permanent nerve damage. Fables credit an earlier practitioner, **Saetacaeia-Viamana**, with deriving the **Shawl of the Sun** — a forbidden art of burning ice-memory clean at the cost of the caster's own remembering — by pressing the Tooth against corrupted ice.
    - **Grandmother Deep** collected the Tooth during the Abyss Collapse Tide, when the Wake-Singers lost three shamans and their attention simultaneously. Less theft than opportunistic acquisition.
    - **Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss** of the **☽'shadow Covens' Order**, a Nightshelf esoteric society, wore the Tooth in a bone cage at her throat wrapped in ash-gray thread. It blazed when Alnae~ Oss gave her life holding back a corrupted fire-core sealed beneath Terrace Momiou.
    - **Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane**, a Nightshelf artificer, restored the Tooth after one of its losses. *Restored* is a careful word — the Tooth was unchanged. Only its wielder came back different. ☽'Milucaum~ was later dispersed in the casting of Grulkzul Omega Strike.
    
    ## Military Deployment
    
    During the **Shattered-Spire Assault** — the orca assault on Aurora Stack — the Wake-Singers focused their hunt-songs through the Tooth to weaponize the colony's own crystalline architecture through resonance. The Tooth survived the Grulkzul Omega Strike that ended the assault. Its wielders did not.
    
    The Tooth's resonance carries farther than intended. The crystal spires of **Promenade Hei**, a penguin surface colony, answer at matching frequencies. Corruption has spread through those spires along the resonance lines. Ice-readers at the Shattered-Spire casting site report a corruption signature matching the Tooth's frequency — a resonance persisting in the ice-memory of Aurora Stack's lower terraces. I have confirmed this independently at depth.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    **Tidescream** holds the Tooth now. Young, ambitious. She has been speaking to something in the pressure-dark for three tides, answering questions no one asks her. The Wake-Singers observe her with the certainty of the inevitable. She has not walked into the depths yet.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771575050861_0", anchor: "officially forgotten — a designation whose implications I leave to scholars of orca liturgical suppression", text: "Not paradox but mechanism. The orca practice of ritual forgetting — preserving a name in the oldest pressure-songs while stripping it from active liturgy — removes the name from use without destroying the record. It remains in the deep structure of the song, audible to those trained to hear the undertones. The name is not lost. It is buried. The distinction is load-bearing.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575050861_1", anchor: "The first lasted four days before the compulsion took her", text: "Orca pressure-songs do not measure in penguin time-units. 'Four days' and 'a week' are translations, and someone chose those numbers. The original cadences are tidal, not diurnal.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575050861_2", anchor: "Less theft than opportunistic acquisition", text: "I was being diplomatic and should not have been. Grandmother Deep is a primordial shaper. The Tooth was carved from her god's jaw; she carried it in her own. Her relationship to this relic is not custodial — it is anatomical. 'Acquisition' frames a divine matriarch's bond to sacred bone as a property transaction because the entry required neutral register. The Wake-Singers did not lose the Tooth during the Abyss Collapse Tide. Grandmother Deep simply reminded everyone whose jaw it came from.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575050861_3", anchor: "The Tooth's chain of possession is tangled", text: "More tangled than written. The registry names the Midnight Claws, the Icebound Exchange, and Collective☽ Of Led∴merch as bearers. I could not source these periods and omitted them rather than guess. The Claws' possession coincides with Shadow-Broker Nyla's tenure. I will not speculate until I have seen the ice.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575050861_4", anchor: "She has not walked into the depths yet", text: "Yet. Three before her. The same pattern: curiosity, communion, descent. Tidescream is answering questions no one asks, and the shamans around her are not intervening because intervention is not part of their theology. They are witnessing. This entry will outlast her. I would like that to matter, and I know that it does not.", type: :commentary, display: :full
